name: babysit
version: "@VERSION@"
origin: sysutils/babysit
comment: Run a command detached, log it, and return early if it stalls
maintainer: matthew@mcgov.dev
www: https://gitlab.com/mowws/babysit
prefix: /usr/local
licenselogic: single
licenses: [MIT]
categories: [sysutils]
desc: <<EOD
babysit runs a command in the background under a babysitter process, echoes
its output and writes it to a per-process log. It returns early when an
expected line appears, when the command stops producing output, or after a
timeout, and leaves the command running in every case.

babysitd does the housekeeping for those logs. See babysitd(8), section
WITHOUT SYSTEMD, for how to run it from cron.
EOD
